emSign Root CA - G1 (eMudhra Technologies Limited), the root that zfin.org's certificate chains to, through
InCommon Intermediate CA - OVG2C and emSign Root TLS CA - G1.

Trusted for the zfin.org downloads of scripts/fetch_raw_sources.sh and nothing else, at the owner's request of
4 November 2026 ("add those ZFIN back to the trusted certificates please"). The script checks this file's SHA-256
fingerprint against the one it pins before every use, and adds it to the default CA bundle for those two fetches only.

Why it is needed: Ubuntu's ca-certificates 20260816ubuntu0.24.04.1 no longer ships this root, and
/etc/ca-certificates.conf lists it as deselected ("!mozilla/emSign_Root_CA_-_G1.crt"), so curl cannot verify zfin.org.
A session of 24 October 2026 added it to that container's trust store, which did not outlive the container.

Source: mozilla/emSign_Root_CA_-_G1.crt in Ubuntu's ca-certificates 20240203 (noble/main), fetched with
apt-get download on 4 November 2026; the package's SHA-256 matched the archive's signed index
(641de77d8f142cfd62a1a6f964ba67b20754d3337c480efb529d086075a06c9a). zfin.org's served leaf verifies against this root
alone with the intermediates the server sends (openssl verify, 4 November 2026).

SHA-256 fingerprint 40:F6:AF:03:46:A9:9A:A1:CD:1D:55:5A:4E:9C:CE:62:C7:F9:63:46:03:EE:40:66:15:83:3D:C8:C8:D0:03:67
Valid 18 February 2018 to 18 February 2043. Text outside the BEGIN and END lines is ignored by openssl and curl.
